flowchart TB
  accTitle: Reachability determines collection eligibility
  accDescr: A runtime root reaches a cache, which strongly references a small view, which retains a large backing buffer. Separately, objects X and Y reference each other but have no root path. The rooted chain stays reachable; the isolated cycle is eligible for tracing collection.
  R["Runtime root"] -->|Strong reference| M["Cache"]
  M -->|Entry| V["Small view"]
  V -->|Retains storage| B["Large backing buffer"]
  X["Unreachable object X"] --> Y["Unreachable object Y"]
  Y --> X
  class R control;
  class B pending;
  class X,Y neutral;

  classDef control fill:#F5F3FF,stroke:#7C3AED,color:#111827;
  classDef neutral fill:#F3F4F6,stroke:#4B5563,color:#111827;
  classDef success fill:#DCFCE7,stroke:#15803D,color:#111827;
  classDef pending fill:#FFFBEB,stroke:#B45309,color:#111827;
  classDef failure fill:#FEE2E2,stroke:#B91C1C,color:#111827;

